.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="For distinct odd primes p, q, \left(\frac{p}{q}\right)\left(\frac{q}{p}\right) = (-1)^{\frac{p-1}{2}\frac{q-1}{2}}: whether p is a square mod q is tied to whether q is a square mod p. The plot tabulates the Legendre symbol for odd primes below 100; reflecting in the diagonal flips the sign exactly when both primes are 3 \bmod 4.">

